{"availability":"available","full":"Amogh21hh/atlas-finance-game","name":"atlas-finance-game","description":"Distressed-corporate turnaround simulator merging Merton distance-to-default, Altman Z-score and Bayesian lender belief into a 12-quarter decision engine. Python · Streamlit · Plotly.","category":"Finance","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-05-29T11:23:17Z","updated":"2026-05-31T00:18:10Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://atlas-finance-game.streamlit.app","topics":["altman-z-score","bayesian-inference","corporate-finance","credit-risk","distressed-debt","financial-modeling","fintech","merton-model","python","quantitative-finance","restructuring","streamlit"],"demo":"https://atlas-finance-game.streamlit.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:31.233Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:31.233Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:31.233Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T09:07:31.233Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Adversarial Turnaround under Liquidity And Sovereign-stress. A 12-quarter, gamified corporate-distress simulator. You play the Chief Restructuring Officer of Albion Industrial PLC — a UK mid-cap industrial firm at BB / Negative Outlook with one covenant breach already on the tape.","This is not a stock tracker, not a textbook DCF, and not a budget app. It is an interactive decision engine that fuses three pieces of corporate-finance theory that rarely sit on the same canvas:","Layered on top is an Eisenberg-Noe-style supply-chain contagion module — when sovereign or supplier shocks occur, the probability of follow-on shocks in linked countries is re-weighted upward, so distress propagates non-linearly through the network."],"features":["Merton structural credit risk — the canonical distance-to-default model from option pricing theory, used here to price the firm's own default probability quarter-by-quarter.","